<h3>6) Data Visualization Using Python</h3>
<p>Data visualization is one of the most important aspects data analysts and engineers use. Graphs and plots help data engineers understand the various parameters of data and how they vary.</p>
<p>Matplotlib is the best Python library for data visualization. It provides a wide range of 2D plots, such as lines, bars, scatter plots, histograms, etc. Let’s study Matplotlib in detail.</p>
<p>To install this library, you can use the “pip” command. </p>
<p>Follow the instructions below on your command line.</p>
<p><strong>C:\Users\prana>pip install matplotlib</strong></p>
<p>Let’s see a few plots one by one:</p>
<p><strong>Line Plot:</strong> A line plot is a plot in which data is represented in series on a number line, with each value being the frequency.</p>
<p>In the below picture, we first import the Matplotlib library. Then you define values on the x and y axes and plot the line plot using the plt.plot(x,y) function.</p>
